1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,800
All right, so while you guys were off doing dumb things like being a rock, getting nosebleeds, or messing with ingredients, I managed to find some patterns in the dungeon's changes.

2
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:13,500
You make it sound like I wanted to turn to stone!

3
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:14,820
Yeah, give us a break.

4
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,820
Those three days were very productive.

5
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:17,900
Uh-huh.

6
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:21,720
When one place gets blocked, another opens up.

7
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:23,500
And that happens over and over.

8
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:27,460
The number of doors, furniture, and building types doesn't change.

9
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:30,200
The houses won't become cemeteries.

10
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:33,740
The walls move in a clockwise spiral at set intervals.

11
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:36,780
And all the statues are in a fixed position.

12
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,560
And then, based on other things.

13
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:44,720
I recognize this road!

14
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:47,500
I'm pretty sure that's the house where we ate the dragon.

15
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:49,520
Chill, Chuck, you're incredible!

16
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:52,140
Hey, just doing my job.

17
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:55,460
Hey, wait, isn't this road...

18
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:57,620
So she remembers it.

19
00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:00,200
We got separated from Fallon here.

20
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,800
Only a trail of blood's been left behind.

21
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:05,900
If they notice the trail, they'll get worked up.

22
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:08,120
How am I gonna handle that?

23
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:09,600
Laios, look there!

24
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:11,700
Wait a second.

25
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:13,000
Listen, you guys!

26
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:17,220
I know there are lots of things to worry about, but for now, we should probably return to the surface?

27
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:27,060
This was where the dragon's corpse was supposed to be, wasn't it?

28
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:30,040
Yeah, but it's been cleared away with no remains.

29
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,160
That hole in the wall over there.

30
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,860
Pretty sure it's from when the red dragon fell down after we got the best of it.

31
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:38,660
It looks almost completely sealed up now.

32
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:45,020
The eye of the mage is quickly approaching.

33
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,260
Don't just yell all of a sudden!

34
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:51,240
But I just saw...

35
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:51,440
Huh?

36
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:52,440
Uh...

37
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:54,120
Huh?

38
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:56,060
Mahana's sickness again, maybe?

39
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:57,040
Again?

40
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:01,820
Ever since I used that healing magic, I've been hallucinating and hearing things.

41
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:03,140
Hearing things?

42
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:04,920
I'm not sure if that's a symptom.

43
00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:06,580
What was it you heard?

44
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:09,360
Oh, it said the eye of the mage approaches.

45
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:11,380
The eye of the mage, huh?

46
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:14,140
That must mean...

47
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:19,500
I'm hearing wings.

48
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:20,720
That small dragon.

49
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:22,060
We need to go and hide.

50
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:23,460
Hide where exactly?

51
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:25,300
Yeah, there's nowhere for us to take cover.

52
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:26,820
We've gotta run, Marcel.

53
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,240
Not yet.

54
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,140
If we need to hide...

55
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,440
We go in the wall!

56
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:36,540
Come on!

57
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:37,680
Hurry up, you two!

58
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:39,020
What is she?

59
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:40,840
It's another one of her magic spells?

60
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:56,920
Tell me, Marcel.

61
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:59,320
That magic you used...

62
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,720
What the hell was that?

63
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:01,160
Huh?

64
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:05,820
Wait, cleaners?

65
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:06,880
Excuse me?

66
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:08,520
Dungeon cleaners.

67
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,620
They're vital creatures to the dungeon.

68
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,960
Basically, they clean trash and repair places that have been destroyed.

69
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:14,960
Uh-huh.

70
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:18,800
The wall wasn't fully restored, so I assumed it hadn't hardened yet.

71
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:21,480
This part is the original wall.

72
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:23,560
And the cleaners start down here!

73
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:24,720
And the floor.

74
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:28,340
They've even reconstructed it with the wear and tear a normal road would have.

75
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,720
You'd never be able to tell the difference.

76
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:32,520
Huh?

77
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:37,500
What the hell are these gross little things crawling all over the ground?

78
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:38,780
Disgusting.

79
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:41,160
These are also cleaners.

80
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:44,480
Any dungeon that didn't have these little guys would fall apart immediately.

81
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:46,440
And thankfully, they're harmless.

82
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:48,240
No, they're not.

83
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:51,780
These pesky little critters are always trying to chew up my tent.

84
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:55,640
They start destroying whatever they feel is in the way.

85
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,580
Guess that includes your tent, Senshi.

86
00:03:57,580 --> 00:04:01,420
But they're here to eat the dragon's corpse and the rubble from the blast.

87
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,160
They appear when the dungeon receives damage

88
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:07,420
and use their secretions to stop any further damage.

89
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:10,480
Then they proceed to eat the debris around the area.

90
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:11,920
They're not picky.

91
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:16,300
After that, they use more secretions to cover up holes they find

92
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:18,720
and restore the dungeon to its original form.

93
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:21,760
It's the same way living beings heal themselves.

94
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,380
To put it another way,

95
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:26,180
think of it like how our immune system removes bacteria.

96
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:27,760
Yeah, I'd rather not.

97
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:30,540
The way all that works sure feels like some type of magic.

98
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,560
Amazing, right?

99
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:32,840
Criminy.

100
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:34,260
What the hell's next?

101
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:35,860
A magical digestive system?

102
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:37,420
If that was really a thing,

103
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:39,060
I wonder what food a dungeon would eat.

104
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:43,680
I'm glad the blood trail wasn't there anymore.

105
00:04:44,340 --> 00:04:47,740
Hey, let's continue on before another change happens.

106
00:04:56,180 --> 00:05:04,900
It's the stairs! Yay!

107
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:08,800
Finally, we can get out of this place.

108
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:09,840
All right.

109
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:12,480
Now's about the time we should start doing that thing.

110
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:13,780
Yeah, good point.

111
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,120
Let's do that.

112
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:16,180
What the...

113
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:17,820
Oh, right.

114
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:18,660
Now I get it.

115
00:05:18,660 --> 00:05:28,820
Wait, you guys meant preparing a meal?

116
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:31,600
I really don't think there are any tentacles on these stairs.

117
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:32,580
Say that sooner!

118
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:35,020
You just like wearing that, don't you?

119
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:35,620
Hell no!

120
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:40,060
We've got tons of different ingredients.

121
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:42,280
I'm having a hard time deciding what to make.

122
00:05:43,540 --> 00:05:45,220
Maybe I'll use that new thing.

123
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:46,700
Cook the barley.

124
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:49,400
Is that what we picked up from the third floor?

125
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:52,960
I've been holding on to it in case we ran out of food since it keeps well.

126
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:55,160
The cockatrice meat,

127
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:57,060
the dryad fruit,

128
00:05:57,180 --> 00:05:59,200
and the mandrake along with its leaves.

129
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:01,800
Chop up the depetrification herb.

130
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:04,580
Season all that and fry it.

131
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:08,480
Now, stuff some barley rice into the hollowed-out brick.

132
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,540
Top it with the rest and put the brick over the fire.

133
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:13,940
And then...

134
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:15,400
What is that thing?

135
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,400
This here's a cockatrice egg.

136
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,760
I'm glad I brought it along with us,

137
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:24,120
but it's pretty dang difficult to use.

138
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,920
Finally, add the egg sauce over top,

139
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:30,800
and it's ready.

140
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:35,480
Whoa, what is this?

141
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:36,420
This looks tasty.

142
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:39,100
If I had stayed petrified longer,

143
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,340
would Senshi have used me to make this?

144
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:48,300
I love this barley rice.

145
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:50,920
Go on and try stabbing the spoon into the bowl.

146
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:57,880
I took a couple bricks made by dungeon cleaners and carved them out.

147
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,520
Then does that mean the bowl's edible, too?

148
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,020
This is great.

149
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:03,900
Thanks, Senshi.

150
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:04,860
What's it taste like?

151
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:09,820
What's it taste like?

152
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:12,080
At first, it just tasted like dirt.

153
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:14,100
But now that it's settling in,

154
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:17,300
it's like a magical mixture of cabbage worm, iron, and lemon.

155
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:19,700
Those are very different things, Laios.

156
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,440
It's pretty hard to describe it properly.

157
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:25,500
Are you sure it's okay to be eating magical creatures?

158
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,900
You'll hear things and get nosebleeds again.

159
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:30,300
What are those hallucinations?

160
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:31,420
Hmm.

161
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:34,480
When we make it back, you should see a doctor.

162
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:35,600
Or a shrink.

163
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:36,300
Why?

164
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:38,660
Do you think this is some kind of illness?

165
00:07:38,660 --> 00:07:47,400
Wait, is this a hallucination, too?

166
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:48,940
Can you guys see this thing?

167
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:51,600
Yeah, I can see it.

168
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:54,460
Hey, uh, not to interrupt.

169
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:56,640
But we're under attack here!

170
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:02,120
Ew.

171
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:03,380
What are you wearing?

172
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,340
Is it the skin of a frog?

173
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:08,660
You know, I think the horns on this one's helmet

174
00:08:08,660 --> 00:08:09,820
are just for decoration.

175
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:11,720
A child, huh?

176
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:16,260
They could be demons in disguise.

177
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:19,280
Shall we discover their true nature?

178
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:21,540
How about we kill one and see if...

179
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:23,080
Mizaru, that's enough.

180
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:28,020
I know them.

181
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:28,940
Shuro!

182
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,800
It's so good to see you!

183
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:32,620
It's been a while!

184
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:35,220
I never thought we'd meet in a situation like this!

185
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:36,660
What a sprawl world!

186
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:38,160
Did you lose weight?

187
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:47,360
I appreciate it, Shuro.

188
00:08:48,580 --> 00:08:50,620
I'm relieved to see you're doing well, buddy.

189
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:52,360
How overly familiar!

190
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:53,600
Oh, yeah!

191
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:54,540
Before I forget.

192
00:08:55,380 --> 00:08:56,940
First up, Senshi.

193
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:58,080
This is Shuro.

194
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,740
He used to be a member of our party.

195
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:01,240
Who is this Shuro?

196
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,040
One of the best fighters I've ever seen.

197
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:03,680
Is he referring to Lord Toshiro?

198
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,720
Not to mention he's about the only person who'd call me a friend.

199
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:05,900
Toshiro!

200
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:09,960
That's enough standing.

201
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:10,880
Come sit with us.

202
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:12,780
You caught us while we were eating.

203
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:16,020
You and your friend should...

204
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:19,380
That's quite the large group you have.

205
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:22,020
Hey, Kabru.

206
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:23,360
Kabru, aren't they?

207
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:26,780
Nice to meet you.

208
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,900
I believe your name is Laios, right?

209
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:32,360
Yeah.

210
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:33,780
Nice to meet you.

211
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:39,380
I wonder just how long it's been.

212
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:42,220
Hey, Kabru.

213
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:42,980
Hmm?

214
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:44,180
It's them, isn't it?

215
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:45,820
They're the ones who stole our things.

216
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:47,300
What do we do?

217
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:48,540
Hmm.

218
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:50,600
We don't do anything.

219
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:51,080
Huh?

220
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:53,440
Then why did we bother coming all this way?

221
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:53,560
Hmm.

222
00:09:58,160 --> 00:09:59,740
I wanted to meet him in person.

223
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:00,900
Huh?

224
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:04,380
I doubt there's any point in asking about the jewels.

225
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:07,880
There wasn't any guilt on his face when he saw us.

226
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:11,640
So either he forgot, we blamed the wrong people,

227
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:14,160
the jewels themselves were a trap from the beginning,

228
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:15,960
or all of the above.

229
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:17,680
Did we come here for nothing?

230
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,020
Not at all.

231
00:10:19,540 --> 00:10:20,820
Give me more time to observe.

232
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:24,040
Aren't you curious about how their party got this far?

233
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:26,280
Or what they might be planning to do next?

234
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:27,580
Because I am.

235
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:32,060
So, I'm assuming you guys have been on this floor for a while now, huh?

236
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,100
That's right.

237
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:35,980
We've been going in circles trying to get out,

238
00:10:36,220 --> 00:10:37,680
but we keep getting turned around.

239
00:10:38,180 --> 00:10:40,060
We got pretty lost in this place, too.

240
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:43,540
Lucky for us, Chilchuk discovered a pattern to the changes,

241
00:10:43,860 --> 00:10:45,740
and that's how we managed to make it this far.

242
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:46,840
That's so.

243
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:49,480
This is unrelated, but...

244
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:50,120
Wow, Cheryl.

245
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:54,560
You're more depraved than I thought.

246
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:55,980
Are they your other plans?

247
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:57,220
You've been busy, huh?

248
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:00,220
They're merely family,

249
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:02,320
but they're skilled at fighting.

250
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:05,680
I'm sorry I left the party.

251
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:09,620
You see, once I realized she wasn't on the surface,

252
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:12,320
I did what I thought would be the best way

253
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,840
for me to get back into the dungeon,

254
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:15,960
so I could start searching for her.

255
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,800
My apologies.

256
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:18,900
It's fine.

257
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,020
We understand.

258
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:23,880
Although, I'm surprised that you went back in immediately.

259
00:11:24,580 --> 00:11:26,220
Don't you think that was a bit rash?

260
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,120
What if somebody were to get hurt again?

261
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:29,680
It must have crossed your mind.

262
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:33,000
Well, for your information,

263
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:36,860
the four of us were able to defeat the Red Dragon.

264
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:40,200
Wait, the Red Dragon?

265
00:11:41,260 --> 00:11:43,480
And where... where is...

266
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:46,860
Cheryl!

267
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:48,140
My lord!

268
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,140
My lord, I'm begging you,

269
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:52,060
please eat a meal and get proper sleep.

270
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:54,580
At this rate, your body will not last long.

271
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:56,420
You've been pushing yourself that hard?

272
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:59,640
Elias, anyone with eyes can see that he's not doing well.

273
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:02,980
Eating a good meal and getting rest is really important.

274
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:06,680
I have no time for such things.

275
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:10,560
Cheryl, you shouldn't just eat food when you have the time.

276
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:13,300
To have the energy to do what you want to do,

277
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:16,740
you need to eat and sleep when your body tells you that you need it.

278
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:19,860
Let's eat something.

279
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:22,760
While we do, I can fill you in on what's happened.

280
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:25,840
All right, then.

281
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:29,580
Can you prepare a meal for us, Maizaru?

282
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:33,800
It's mealtime!

283
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:35,480
Let us begin preparing!

284
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:37,960
Tade, you go fetch some water.

285
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:38,900
Okay.

286
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:42,640
Hien, Benichidori, you two start preparing the rice.

287
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:45,300
And Ausebi, your job is...

288
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:48,700
To protect our lord from harm.

289
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:51,560
Can't have you adding strange things to the food.

290
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:54,140
I'll go start lighting a fire for you all.

291
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:56,100
Oh my, so thoughtful.

292
00:12:56,100 --> 00:12:58,320
I'll leave that to you then, Dwarf.

293
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,220
Food time, yummy, but...

294
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:02,880
There sure are a lot of people here.

295
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:06,460
It's not good to have this many people all in one place.

296
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:08,740
We should split into three groups.

297
00:13:09,460 --> 00:13:09,700
Hmm.

298
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:11,280
Very well.

299
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:12,540
Oren!

300
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:13,120
Huh?

301
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:13,880
Dwarf!

302
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:14,260
Huh?

303
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:15,280
Frog girl!

304
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:15,820
Frog!

305
00:13:15,820 --> 00:13:19,600
If you're capable of magic, then provide us with a barrier.

306
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:23,100
It's to prevent monsters from disturbing our lord's meal.

307
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:27,220
Well, pleasure to meet you, Miss Frog.

308
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:27,680
Oh.

309
00:13:28,460 --> 00:13:28,980
Same.

310
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:31,480
All right.

311
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:32,820
Let's step away from the group.

312
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:35,040
Ben will tell you everything we've been up to.

313
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:36,640
Let me help.

314
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:37,480
Thanks.

315
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:39,640
Thanks so much, James.

316
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:40,740
So what I'll tell you.

317
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:44,100
In this situation, I think the person in the most danger is...

318
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:46,040
Monsters are yummy.

319
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:47,420
They're the best!

320
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:49,720
Monsters cooking food.

321
00:13:49,860 --> 00:13:50,600
Yum, yum.

322
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:51,500
Eat a lot.

323
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:53,400
I'll kill you.

324
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:54,680
Senshi!

325
00:13:55,180 --> 00:13:56,460
I'll come out for the fire!

326
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:11,920
Hey, aren't you overdoing it a little bit?

327
00:14:12,340 --> 00:14:13,420
So much smoke.

328
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:17,120
They must have him take a bath after his meal.

329
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:18,260
Here?

330
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:20,840
Why don't you have a seat right over there?

331
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:21,600
Fine.

332
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:23,520
Now hurry and tell me what's happened.

333
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:27,380
Well, after you and Namari left the group, the rest of us...

334
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:28,640
Stick to the main points.

335
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:33,440
We defeated the Red Dragon, then retrieved Falon and brought her back to life.

336
00:14:33,820 --> 00:14:37,540
But then we were attacked by the Mad Mage, and we got separated.

337
00:14:38,340 --> 00:14:44,580
We decided that we couldn't do this on our own, so we were going back to the surface to ask around for some help.

338
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:46,240
But we got lost.

339
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:47,880
You see?

340
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:50,200
That's why I'm glad we ran into you!

341
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:51,960
Please, lend us your strength, Shuro!

342
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:57,200
Mind if I ask a few questions?

343
00:14:58,060 --> 00:15:02,160
The one who created this place is the Mad Mage you mentioned just now, is that correct?

344
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:07,380
There's only been rumors of his existence, and whoever actually saw him never returned.

345
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:10,320
How'd you know it was the Mad Mage you saw?

346
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:14,520
Well, I guess I thought he talked like he fit the part.

347
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:17,380
And how'd you manage to get away from that dangerous situation?

348
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:19,140
That was all Marcille.

349
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:22,860
Oh, she's our magic user, and she held him off.

350
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:23,880
Can you elaborate?

351
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:26,400
Well, uh...

352
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:29,340
Magic isn't really my thing, so I couldn't say.

353
00:15:30,460 --> 00:15:31,540
Oh, I see.

354
00:15:33,540 --> 00:15:35,480
May I ask something too, Lyos?

355
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:35,880
Hmm?

356
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:45,120
Did I see you eating a brick earlier?

357
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:46,000
No!

358
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:47,980
Ah, no, no, no!

359
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,460
It wasn't a brick.

360
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:52,380
We were eating part of a wall that was made of dungeon cleaners.

361
00:15:52,620 --> 00:15:56,060
We left almost everything behind, including food and money, remember?

362
00:15:56,460 --> 00:16:01,260
So for us to traverse the dungeon faster, we've been eating monsters this entire time!

363
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:06,980
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha

364
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:09,260
That's...

365
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:09,800
Hmm?

366
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:13,360
That's actually really interesting.

367
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:16,600
Well, what's the most delicious thing you've had so far?

368
00:16:16,660 --> 00:16:17,840
Man, I don't know.

369
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,080
That's a hard one.

370
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:21,040
Kelpie, Living Armour.

371
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:22,900
You know, it might be the red dragon.

372
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:23,960
No way!

373
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,060
You ate the red dragon that ate your sister?

374
00:16:26,420 --> 00:16:26,680
Yeah.

375
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:28,420
You said living armor.

376
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:29,920
What's even edible on it?

377
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:31,420
That's an excellent question.

378
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:34,800
It's actually a mollusk creature that uses the armor as a shell,

379
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:36,060
just like this sword.

380
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:36,960
Whoa!

381
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:38,620
The cleaners are eating Kensuke!

382
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:40,300
Can't be too careful.

383
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:43,560
By the way, if you're interested in monster meals,

384
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:44,840
we can talk about it whenever.

385
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:47,300
Wow, I appreciate that.

386
00:16:47,660 --> 00:16:48,380
Oh, no.

387
00:16:48,640 --> 00:16:50,720
He's actually serious about this.

388
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:57,040
Anyway, you had mentioned that you had resurrected Fallon.

389
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:59,300
Was she safe the last time you saw her?

390
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:01,100
Uh, yeah.

391
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:02,660
Do you know where she might be?

392
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:05,600
There are many places where you can hide on this floor,

393
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:07,920
but most of them are in orcs' territory.

394
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:08,800
Oh, yeah.

395
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:10,440
The orcs shouldn't be an issue.

396
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:11,420
Oh?

397
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:14,780
What'd they taste like?

398
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:15,720
We didn't eat them.

399
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:16,860
There were some things that happened,

400
00:17:16,940 --> 00:17:18,600
and now we're in a cooperative relationship.

401
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:19,600
Mm-hmm.

402
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:21,800
Co-operative relationship?

403
00:17:22,360 --> 00:17:25,440
Technically, it's an adventurous duty to kill any orcs.

404
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:27,440
Regarding where she is,

405
00:17:27,820 --> 00:17:30,600
it's possible she's on a much deeper floor of the dungeon.

406
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:33,860
The one who kidnapped her may have taken her there.

407
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:35,360
Wait, kidnapped?

408
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:36,460
But why her?

409
00:17:36,740 --> 00:17:38,040
Uh, well...

410
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:41,360
I think telling Shuro would be fine.

411
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:44,520
Sorry, but could I talk with him privately?

412
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:45,380
Sure.

413
00:17:45,580 --> 00:17:46,740
That's not a problem at all.

414
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:55,560
So?

415
00:17:55,560 --> 00:18:04,240
It's not that field ration pellets are bad,

416
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:05,640
but having them every day,

417
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:09,620
I just think you need to have something warm in your belly from time to time.

418
00:18:09,820 --> 00:18:10,560
Cheers to that.

419
00:18:11,020 --> 00:18:13,060
Meals should do a lot more than fill your stomach

420
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:14,620
until the next chance you get to eat.

421
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,220
You know, you're quite sensible for a dwarf.

422
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:20,000
Our lord's been sickly ever since childhood.

423
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,880
His appetite was lacking,

424
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:24,140
and it made everyone around him worry.

425
00:18:25,100 --> 00:18:26,820
However, no matter the situation,

426
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,360
he would always eat the food I prepared for him.

427
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:33,000
Sometimes I'd be summoned to the kitchen in the middle of an assignment.

428
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:35,960
He was such an obedient child growing up

429
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:37,180
that it made me anxious.

430
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:40,220
The only selfish request he's ever made

431
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:41,840
was the one that brought us here.

432
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:43,460
Please, Maizuru.

433
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:46,020
There's someone that I wish to save.

434
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:48,020
Lend me your strength.

435
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:49,340
Oh.

436
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:53,600
To think some northern girl would steal his heart

437
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:54,860
during his training journey.

438
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:57,500
What can I even say to dissuade him?

439
00:18:57,980 --> 00:18:59,780
You really want him to give up?

440
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:02,100
The head of the family bestowed me

441
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:04,160
with the task of looking after the young lord,

442
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:06,660
so I cannot act based on emotion.

443
00:19:07,340 --> 00:19:08,120
In that case,

444
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,900
then what do you think you're doing right now?

445
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:11,820
If you have preserved foods,

446
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,400
there's no need to go through the trouble

447
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:14,680
of preparing a fresh meal.

448
00:19:15,620 --> 00:19:15,940
Hmm?

449
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:18,140
Why do you reckon he ate up

450
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:19,980
all the things you personally made for him?

451
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:22,280
Maybe you didn't realize at the time,

452
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:23,880
but I know what you put in there.

453
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:28,000
A little ingredient called love.

454
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:31,400
What are you saying?

455
00:19:31,780 --> 00:19:33,600
Are you proud of yourself for that one?

456
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:37,480
Although, at this point,

457
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:38,860
I just might give in.

458
00:19:38,860 --> 00:19:41,520
So, depending on how things turn out,

459
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:43,960
perhaps I'll put in a good word for those, too.

460
00:19:49,540 --> 00:19:51,540
Why did the art style change so much?

461
00:19:51,780 --> 00:19:53,940
This depiction might be a bit of a stretch,

462
00:19:54,020 --> 00:19:54,580
don't you think?

463
00:19:55,700 --> 00:19:56,140
Yes.

464
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:57,500
This will suffice.

465
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:58,900
It's ready!

466
00:20:01,780 --> 00:20:02,560
Hurry, dwarf!

467
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:04,480
It's important we have my lord eat this

468
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:05,540
while it's still warm!

469
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:07,100
Oh?

470
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:08,460
You two.

471
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:10,100
Why are you outside?

472
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:12,320
They said they wanted to speak in private.

473
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:15,360
My lord, I'm coming in.

474
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:17,780
My lord!

475
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:20,720
What is going on?

476
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:23,560
Did this man do something?

477
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:26,320
Tell me!

478
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:27,840
I need to know what happened here!

479
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:29,900
Sorry, but we couldn't hear from there.

480
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:32,540
It's black magic.

481
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,320
This man and the others

482
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:36,180
used black magic and monster flesh

483
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:37,560
to revive the northern girl.

484
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:38,560
What?

485
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:42,640
How could you do such a thing?

486
00:20:43,380 --> 00:20:45,040
Do you even know what you have done?

487
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:47,400
People who deal with black magic,

488
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,840
the reasons that they have matter not.

489
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:51,360
They are nothing but criminals!

490
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:54,440
They get locked in dark cells until they die,

491
00:20:54,740 --> 00:20:56,480
and their corpses are never returned.

492
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:58,680
If the western elves find out,

493
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:00,620
then who knows what they'll do to her?

494
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:03,780
That's assuming this leaves the dungeon, Shuro.

495
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:06,380
And you won't tell another soul

496
00:21:06,380 --> 00:21:07,500
about any of this happening.

497
00:21:09,020 --> 00:21:09,580
Right?

498
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:16,540
We had no other options.

499
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:18,780
Please understand.

500
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:22,660
Black magic.

501
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:25,080
This is crazier than I imagined.

502
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:27,540
How's this gonna turn out?

503
00:21:30,620 --> 00:21:57,320
I must locate you as soon as possible.

